  "Question": "Calculate \\((-3/4)\\times(8/9)\\). Write the result as a fraction in simplest form.",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "-2/3",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Opposite signs give a negative product. Multiply the absolute values: \\(3/4\\times8/9=24/36=2/3\\), so the result is \\(-2/3\\).",
